6801-b7ff-4284-afa9-ff20b3760134"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"12703b294b331d4b66ec108f04de4e06ef58447b7851ad02c89b79a97936fd4f","event_uuid":"c4d72ec1-e6fa-436d-9586-6b50691c6178","position":{"commit_sha":"e9819e73f3cee92507b9b557813ec610afeab55a","position":"1787737470445354001-c4d72ec1-e6fa-436d-9586-6b50691c6178"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c5fd20272deeba24079e8f305a3d45b40ca1dfc0e66acf1ef895fdd0aad76a7","event_uuid":"f3a12d4e-75c5-4213-9c95-91f2b97e19b0","position":{"commit_sha":"b34dd06d6f8fef4a0d17a67b952bb8cb5b1fa50d","position":"1787737485875740001-f3a12d4e-75c5-4213-9c95-91f2b97e19b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI (change 2235 ps1) failed: removing the class-name Mutation dispatch made typed dispatch class-identity-sensitive, so cross-loaded Mutation instances (the reconciler loads mutation.py under two sys.modules keys) fell through to the batch path -> AttributeError/'Mutation has no .get' + 'requires pass_id'. Root cause: bare isinstance(x, mut_mod.Mutation) binds one class identity. Fix (ps2): dispatch via an explicit @runtime_checkable declared protocol MutationShape (attributes direction+action) defined in apply_base.py and imported into applier.py -- identity-agnostic, no class-name string (AC4 poison holds), and exactly AC5's 'explicit declared protocol'. A batch dict lacks those attributes so it still routes to the batch path. Validated: census 9 passed; full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler 3579 passed/1 skipped; make lint + make typecheck green; applier 793 LOC (<800).","timestamp":1787729846142795001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LLM-Review ps1 = PASS (+1) with 3 ADVISORY findings; dispositions: (1) batch_dispatch delete_one mutation['key'] vs .get('key'): ACCEPTED as-is. Reverting to .get('key') fails mypy (delete_issue expects str, .get returns Any|None); the old .get passed only via the removed _call_with_retry wrapper's loose typing. A delete batch dict always carries 'key' (built in apply_handlers), so ['key'] is the type-correct fail-fast form; passing None to delete_issue would be the real bug. (2) census AC4 static source-text absence check and (3) AC6 docstring-prose grep flagged as change-detectors: these are the AC4/AC6-MANDATED source-absence + rollback-guidance proofs, complemented by the file's runtime poison tests. Strengthening AC6 into a behavioral 'rollback never calls delete_issue' assertion is deferred to T3 (a735), whose file_impact finalizes this census with full E2E.","timestamp":1787733266750463001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787028432114144001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"42f712bf-5acb-477b-8642-9ad8f72cd224","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7578-ef26-35e5-4792"},{"link_uuid":"0a2eb628-9f4c-4c4a-8c59-e63ff039a864","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e5b7-a5c8-7ff7-4761"},{"link_uuid":"a5b8e07d-cb88-494a-907b-61a95c96077f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f5ca-8725-7eee-4770"}],"description":"## Context\nAfter family cutovers, reachable generic retry, `_best_effort` swallowing, duck-typed dispatch, or duplicate SDK/adapter retry would preserve the original failure class and invite future bypass.\n\n## Outcome\nProve every supported Cloud/DC mutation has exactly one typed coordinator/adapter owner, remove obsolete production fallbacks, and fail unsupported live actions before any effect.\n\n## Plan\n1. Build a dispatch census over every `MutationDirection`/`MutationAction` and Cloud/DC provider route. Require one typed owner or an intentional provider-neutral pre-effect unsupported result.\n2. Remove generic whole-operation retry, `_best_effort` write swallowing, production class-name/duck fallbacks, and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners after their route is covered.\n3. Keep compatibility only at serialized/public read boundaries; tests use explicit protocol fakes.\n4. Add static/string and runtime poison tests that fail when removed helpers remain reachable from production.\n5. Preserve rollback as code/routing reversion plus remote re-observation; never compensate by deleting successful Jira work.\n\n## Testing\nThe census must fail on missing, duplicate, or fallback owners. Effect spies prove unsupported actions fail before local/remote writes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every supported Cloud/DC mutation route has exactly one typed coordinator/adapter owner.\n- [x] Unsupported production actions return a typed provider-neutral error before any effect.\n- [x] Generic whole-operation retry and `_best_effort` write swallowing are unreachable from production.\n- [x] Production class-name/duck dispatch and duplicate SDK/adapter retry owners are unreachable.\n- [x] Tests use explicit declared protocols rather than production fallback paths.\n- [x] Rollback guidance requires re-observation and never remote deletion.\n\n## Out of scope\nFinal output contracts, state advancement, end-to-end validation, and docs.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"Remove legacy generic retry and production dispatch fallbacks; dispatch typed mutations via the declared MutationShape protocol (identity-agnostic)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_base.py","reason":"Home the @runtime_checkable MutationShape declared protocol alongside the mutation-identity loaders it complements."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"Remove obsolete whole-operation retry routes."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","reason":"Complete route ownership census and runtime poison tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3350-90b1-2651-4c50"],["relates_to","7578-ef26-35e5-4792"],["relates_to","e5b7-a5c8-7ff7-4761"],["relates_to","f5ca-8725-7eee-4770"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3350-90b1-2651-4c50","parent_status_uuid":"c4d72ec1-e6fa-436d-9586-6b50691c6178","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp03","coordinator","cleanup","tdd"],"ticket_id":"b81b-8671-3c61-488f","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S5 T1 — Census typed routes and remove legacy write fallbacks","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC6","dd_text":"Complete route census, pre-effect unsupported behavior, fallback removal, protocol fakes, and rollback"}]},"source_event_uuids":["bc0195bd-cb36-48af-873d-6096d3358f28","ccb31553-81f6-462b-bafb-81e5424fc0c0","2a39f3e9-a3e8-4ee2-9d3e-927c5cb1fa5f","42f712bf-5acb-477b-8642-9ad8f72cd224","e8136ed3-85